    "body": "Anne was the one who made the time to get to this first, so his preferences take preference. But to me 7 PRs feels a bit excessive. And GitHub's tooling for reviewing individual commits seems fine to me? You just go to each commit and add review comments.\r\n\r\nIn particular, the first three commits are clearly good. The fourth also looks good.\r\n\r\nFor removing unused variables, some of them seem good but the ones Anne commented on are scary and I'd prefer to investigate them further before deleting, maybe with a tracking issue. So separating that into a separate PR might be worthwhile.\r\n\r\nFor `Editorial: Replace <var> with something else` and `Editorial: Change non-<var> to <var> `, I think it all looks good, with one nit I noted.",
